  "cards": [
    {
      "title": "Different credentials",
      "items": [
        "MDM customer certificates authorize MDM wake notifications. App provider certificates authorize app notifications for their permitted topics.",
        "The MDM vendor signing identity signs customer CSR requests; it is not the credential used to send customer MDM pushes.",
        "The customer retains the CSR private key. The vendor receives the public CSR, and Apple’s portal returns only a certificate. The app-provider flow also combines a downloaded certificate with a locally retained key."
      ],
      "dot": "certificate"
    },
    {
      "title": "Validation and replacement",
      "items": [
        "Managed MDM import validates the returned certificate against its pending private key and stores a ready revision. It does not replace the active runtime credential.",
        "Activate revalidates the ready revision, then commits workflow activation and the reference server’s runtime push row in one transaction. Failed import or activation leaves the active credential unchanged.",
        "Runtime MDM reload retires cached connections after activation. App import commits its separate credential and invalidates its cache; shutdown closes clients."
      ],
      "dot": "certificate"
    },
    {
      "title": "Persistent storage",
      "items": [
        "App push credentials require encryption in persistent state. They are separate from the MDM certificate table and its key-rewrap path."
      ],
      "dot": "storage"
    },
    {
